module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.host_ordered_collection_reaches_an_emitted_artifact

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data host_ordered_collection_reaches_an_emitted_artifact: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "host_ordered_collection_reaches_an_emitted_artifact" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a collection whose iteration order is a HOST fact -- a hash map's keys, a hash set's members -- is iterated straight into an EMITTED ARTIFACT. The emitted bytes then carry a permutation nothing in the program chose, so the artifact's IDENTITY moves while its MEANING does not. Nothing is wrong with any single run's output: every run is a correct rendering of the same graph. What is destroyed is the artifact's usability as an oracle, and that loss is silent at the site that caused it.",

    "RECEIPT, 2026-09-11, in v1.compile emit_dag_artifact and serialize_typed_module, found by session bright-bear-236 on gunbc#11072. Two identical invocations of one binary over one unchanged tree emitted dag-artifact.json with IDENTICAL LENGTH and 2,408 differing comma-separated fields: every $ref node id agreed, and the whole difference was the ORDER of item_registry_keys, fed from map_keys of a host-ordered map at both sites. The finder was measuring typecheck memory and tried to use artifact equality as an equivalence oracle for their own change; the diff reported a difference whether or not their change caused one, and they nearly reported a regression against their own work before running the binary twice against itself.",

    "RECEIPT, EARLIER AND THE SAME CLASS, gunbc#10941: re-export lines emitted in unordered-set order, repaired by sorting at the key. Two instances in two emitters is what makes this a class rather than a site.",

    "WHAT IT COSTS, AND THE COST IS NOT THE BYTES. Every byte-equality oracle downstream of an unstable artifact -- a regen fixed point, a drift observer, an emitted-closure identity claim, a behavioural receipt comparing two emissions -- loses the ability to distinguish CHANGED from REORDERED. Such an oracle then fails in whichever direction its defaults point: one that compares reports perpetual change and is eventually ignored or widened; one that does not compare reports nothing at all. In the 2026-09-11 receipt it was the second: NO gate compared dag-artifact.json, so nothing was reading green by accident -- the artifact simply had no reader, and the first consumer to reach for it as an oracle is the one who paid.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: at every site whose result reaches an EMITTED BYTE, ask what the ORDER of each collection it iterates is a fact ABOUT. If the answer is the host's hashing rather than the program's declaration, the artifact's identity is unstable whether or not anyone has noticed. The mechanical tell in this substrate is a key-list constructor whose PrimitiveTraversalOrderFact is HostUnspecifiedOrder -- map_keys, map_values -- on a path into a rendered string. THE REPAIR IS AT THE KEY AND NEVER AT THE TEXT: ordering by a stable key (sorted_map_keys, CanonicalOrder) makes the emitted order a fact about the data, while sorting the emitted output afterwards is a second authority over the same bytes that the next emitted field will not inherit.",

    "THE CHEAP CONTROL THAT SETTLES IT, stated because the finder's own note is the most transferable part: run the producer TWICE against itself BEFORE trusting any artifact comparison. It costs one extra run and answers whether the oracle is valid at all. An equality control needs its positive control beside it -- one perturbed input that MUST change the bytes -- because equality alone is satisfied by a producer blind to its input.",

    "CEILING AND NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER. Found at MITIGATABLE: the instability was observable only by running the emitter twice and nothing did. Raised to MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE for this artifact by the dag-artifact-identity rider on the required generated-artifact phase (build lane, every pull request and merge_group; it rode the regen-fixed-point phase until that phase was deleted by operator ruling 2026-10-04, and moved rather than lapsed, so the rung is unchanged), which emits a committed fixture twice and compares bytes, with a one-declaration-larger specimen as the positive control. It is NOT structural: nothing stops the next emitted field from reading map_keys, and the control's subject is one artifact rather than the emitted population. CEILING is STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED, and the trigger names the CAPABILITY rather than an artifact: a compile-time decision that refuses a HostUnspecifiedOrder traversal on any path reaching an emitted byte -- the order fact is already declared per primitive in std.primitive_identity, so what is missing is the reachability judgment that consumes it, not the classification. RENDERING SUBCLASS, 2026-10-01: interpreted rendering is STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE to put in host order (Display has no HamtMap-order constructor; it can only render through canonical_entries), and emitted rendering is refused before any artifact exists, so the rendering path is no longer the floor of this class; iteration through map_keys and map_values stays MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE at the gate, which is the class minimum.",

    "RECEIPT, 2026-10-01, RENDERING (node adhoc-77383faf-d07, jolly-hawk-293; census by sleek-ibex-207, routed by jolly-boar-500). to_string(map), string interpolation of a map and Debug formatting rendered Value::Map entries in HamtMap RandomState order, re-randomised per process, so any .dag program that rendered a map produced per-process bytes, and the gate did not classify rendering at all. RULING (neat-boar-16, deep-ferret-305): render in the CANONICAL order through ONE authority, not refuse -- refusing every map rendering would over-prohibit (DESIGN section 4d) a fact that can be constructed (section 5). The authority is std.algebra TotalOrder (OrderedRing and Field now compose it rather than restating compare), realized in the seed by v1_interpreter canonical_content_cmp over one ContentView that Value and PortableValue both expose, so the portable encoding (#12895, portable_value_cmp) and rendering share one order: kind rank by ContentKind declaration order, floats by IEEE 754-2019 section 5.10 totalOrder, records and variants by spelling then payload (the spelling stand-in is rostered on gunbc.guarantee_stall variant_owner_identity_stall). DISCRIMINATING CONTROL: v1_interpreter::canonical_render_order_tests rendered_map_bytes_are_equal_across_two_processes and debug_map_bytes_are_equal_across_two_processes, each RED (\"two processes rendered one map differently\") with the HamtMap-order Display restored and GREEN with the canonical one; value_and_portable_carriers_agree_on_every_pair is the one-order differential over a corpus spanning every kind pair, empty and non-empty collections, nested maps and sets, NaN and both zeros.",

    "THE EMITTED HALF IS A REFUSAL, AND WHY. The emitted realization had no map rendering at all -- interpolation lowers to format!(\"{}\") and im::HashMap has no Display -- so emitted map rendering died in rustc as an untyped E0277 rather than as per-process bytes. v1.compiler emit_rust emitted_map_rendering_refusal now refuses it typed and located. Building an emitted canonical rendering fails the v1 admission test (no v2 source renders a map; none could compile), so it is a declared frontier, trigger: a v2 source renders a compound value (ruling deep-ferret-305). SORT PARITY: emitted sorted_map_keys and sort_by order by K's derived Ord, which for generated records and enums is DECLARATION order; the interpreter admits only Str, Int and Bool keys (v1_interpreter admit_emitted_ord_keys, where the canonical order IS the native Ord, control canonical_order_is_native_ord_on_emitted_admitted_key_kinds) and refuses every other key kind typed. sort_by previously answered Equal for unrecognised pairs through cmp_values -- an absorbing fallback that silently disagreed with the emitted sort -- and cmp_values is deleted. The emitted side still ACCEPTS record- and enum-keyed sorts the interpreter refuses: the two admit different programs, loudly rather than silently, and that divergence closes when the emitted sort consumes the canonical order.",

    "CENSUS OF REMAINING HOST-ORDER PATHS (seed interpreter, every site that iterates a Value::Map's entries): Display and Debug -- canonical; portable_value_from_ctx_at -- canonical (#12895); value_hash, eval_recompute frames and account_value -- commutative folds, order-independent by construction; map_keys and map_values -- HostUnspecifiedOrder, refused by v2.lens.determinism determinism_compile_gate. to_string is now a declared primitive with a CanonicalOrder traversal fact (std.primitive_identity primitive_to_string_traversal) instead of Deterministic-by-non-membership. So the gate goes red on every remaining host-order primitive path; string interpolation is syntax rather than a primitive call and is covered by the shared Display realization, not by the primitive join.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
